[{"id":"VRCE-1-41-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":1,"english":"When Sagara had bowed to the influence of Time, the subjects selected the righteous Ansumat for their king.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6e8504a130de4b92b84edbb3f0df8c47ac837721afd5520fc11d52078ec97530","compact":"2b87bd9228aeb89b6d0c6ad5dd8fe2e4c35853da3f40068c46f2cd98fdefb59e","nasal":"09b6e9aaaea7bdb6c1b6715873e61ceecb1f0c1ca22dc3ba39cb6107fb322eae"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":2,"english":"O descendant of Raghu, Ansumat proved a great ruler. And his son, the celebrated Dilīpa, was also a great king.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e12cbade4dd3bafb64a2dee626100266852b1bbbea16def3dc65fb85a5f38549","compact":"82b59934edcc5d6b59f97e774b2d14559713ba31ecc07690164ab840551db6c1","nasal":"bad95591a9754c0240c4c14e27c56fce4e7d2698e9da292adca525c2974085e0"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":3,"english":"O Raghu's son, consigning to Dilipa his kingdom, Ansumat entered upon rigid austerities on the romantic summit of the Himavat.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"341a061e2a922279fa09e1149bc8fd3c51b28c19debf6568dacf41a58cb47116","compact":"de081cfdecb7a8ec22dbf02facdb79bea02ff6f6a1d347124d0da74690836c75","nasal":"274daae629297380126f1fb1c9139396e0e212db2e96ce93e0d8303ad8530ddc"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":4,"english":"Having for the space of thirty-two you sand years carried on austerities in the woods, that highly famous one, crowned with the wealth of asceticism, attained the celestial regions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d8cb89902f68e9ad07edded5fb4e7930a0ab6d44cd6f7107bfd9cd72a2ec9103","compact":"fb69399f5ee596d328213e51232bb09bb0afaeb7450b428043bdcceec9c75c83","nasal":"fb69399f5ee596d328213e51232bb09bb0afaeb7450b428043bdcceec9c75c83"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":5,"english":"The exceedingly powerful Dilīpa, hearing of the destruction of his grand-fathers, was stricken with grief; yet he could not ascertain his grandfathers, was stricken with grief; yet he could not ascertain his course about it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"564802cd65689d9bea1e1f953bdfa0758ac113bf4b184903c5fbac8e4fe60c82","compact":"763bd949b00173f35c868cab8ebcb799681d0493ab6b057f7382c21bf80e4b07","nasal":"763bd949b00173f35c868cab8ebcb799681d0493ab6b057f7382c21bf80e4b07"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":6,"english":"He constantly thought as to how Gangă could be brought down, how to perform their watery rites, and how to deliver them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c942c71d489bba0d2dd74692863ed7ad020ad3f4eee6442a7f0e1ff0d0c617d9","compact":"8155a49f2fbc30840370dc19404e4a0400f493d491af36c66a7705206e7f3c92","nasal":"0f159fbdb8427f75f43ccbfa9d79501e64efb7dedfaddb33edab70b78a9a806f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":7,"english":"As that pious one furnished with selfknowledge was always meditating upon this, an eminently virtuous son was born to him named Bhagiratha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0bdfa1789617f58410b3b372554dde04c17603bee00273fc7e20341a0f32cf49","compact":"be627c60ac8a58ab18148e6bb1f7b7d4bd67584639effaa86b5a00d110e5ca00","nasal":"b9db326e3809d9817dcfb3b7302d8c02adbd8e5625836bdf74795c7f8a763717"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":8,"english":"Performing numerous sacrifices, the mighty king Dilīpa reigned for thirty thousand years.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"31dd24d5e8787fd2b2e72b01d924d5ec6c4ced4824d7594229ebcf3be46c2596","compact":"b92ff8519d64cf0188da18b29705b164543c2c0d16a53a7f754c7571396faa02","nasal":"96dbd8771b0f581cd11b198ff1146b378863cdb0c75b47b475ffef43d2578c82"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":9,"english":"And without having arrived at any definite decision in regard to their deliverance, the king, O puissant one, being attacked with an ailment, breathed his last.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bc03ffa32568d60eefa3ae90c85216fcafeae13091ba0691cac9e0c26826b689","compact":"3e99224da00d1b5abbfa9fd0f5886f7d3d8a2b9584802d1942e8d4b33ecccbf0","nasal":"3e99224da00d1b5abbfa9fd0f5886f7d3d8a2b9584802d1942e8d4b33ecccbf0"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":10,"english":"Having sprinkled his son Bhagiratha in the way of installing him in the kingdom, that prime of men, the king, by virtue of his own acts, repaired to the region of Indra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.885,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"00f9dc5c20724646120a8e9465c078271ad2fd4ee820a410e04ceaff9b15c8be","compact":"ab7746bad0c6f4d99701de73058030b15a9fa4fdd659db150eb6640eb87bd5ce","nasal":"f9d9480ba09e75db96c0bb8c54014b5d7a45ec3cad96fa255622b325de066ec3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":11,"english":"O descendant of Raghu, that royal saint Bhagiratha was possessed of righteousness. And being without issue, and desiring to obtain it, the mighty monarch consigned his kingdom and his subjects to the care of his counsellors, and engaged in bringing down Gangā.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.559,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"06feef6f04bd4767251992f37ae759c78621009ed8b932ac68ea8b32eedf7ad6","compact":"2aba355200b7b0e8acf6b8eec98c6b2339e607097f034c70ff9f87733a38b9e5","nasal":"9b28c5d1510811804deb7fd98d5fb9c4103b467f047f85acb0d563b70adab7d1"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":12,"english":"O descendant of Raghu, that royal saint Bhagiratha was possessed of righteousness. And being without issue, and desiring to obtain it, the mighty monarch consigned his kingdom and his subjects to the care of his counsellors, and engaged in bringing down Gangā. And, O Raghu's descendant, restraining his senses, and eating once a month, and surrounding himself with five fires, and with arms upraised, he for a long lapse of time performed austerities at Gokarna. And as he was performing his terrible austerities, a thousand years rolled away.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.484,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-11","DUTT-1-42-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3cfa257de0d85f210d9689ad56d44b36c0570c79445eb582bbc1ef2775795cee","compact":"8462872abdf1b61fde960331f4da33bdfb209f54a59992ab0c2abfc4612b385c","nasal":"6f3f9f5584949e434013f5ee4aed2f188f188b193187444c03b127a053fd1ba4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-41-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":41,"verse":13,"english":"And, O Raghu's descendant, restraining his senses, and eating once a month, and surrounding himself with five fires, and with arms upraised, he for a long lapse of time performed austerities at Gokarna. And as he was performing his terrible austerities, a thousand years rolled away. And thereat that possessor of the six attributes and lord of all creatures, Brahmā, was well pleased with that high-souled monarch. And presenting himself together with the celestials, the Grand-sire thus spoke to the high-souled Bhagiratha engaged in austerities.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.381,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-42-12","DUTT-1-42-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1041013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"171945d6d5f97e4258650df0522800a29